# Quickstart

The smallest complete use of the library: smooth a series of samples.

## Try it on your PC

[`examples/host/`](../examples/host/README.md) is a complete program; from the repository root:

```bash
cmake -S examples/host -B build-example && cmake --build build-example && ./build-example/xmpl100_host_example
```

## 1. Add the library

```bash
git submodule add https://github.com/@ORG@/@REPO@.git external/@REPO@
```

```cmake
add_subdirectory(external/@REPO@)
target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE xmpl100::xmpl100)
```

## 2. Use it

```cpp title="main.cpp"
--8<-- "tests/docs/quickstart.cpp:quickstart"
```

1. `Initialize()` sets the window; a window of 0 or above the capacity is `InvalidArgument`.
2. `Push()` adds a sample; NaN is refused with `InvalidArgument` and changes nothing.
3. `Average()` is the mean of the window, or `Empty` before the first sample.

This example is built by the host CI, so it compiles against the current headers.

